{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdmCDozNZkDFE5ssbChh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a working spec of Button, TextField, StatusBar and HomeIndicator, and the block on the phone-number sheet dump fails at dump line 8:32 with \"cannot convert symbol to string\". My take: the four failing nodes (1:23 Button, 1:26 Text Field, 1:33 Status Bar, 1:44 Home Indicator) are instance-like nodes, and 1:46 (COMPONENT) reads fine, so the difference sits in instance handling rather than in paint(). A cautious read of unknown fields is the shortest path: for each of the 4 nodes, wrap each of type, name, characters, fills (with color hex), fontSize, cornerRadius and child count in its own try/catch, and fall back to a placeholder string when one read fails. That a read can fail while JSON.stringify quietly turns a bad value into null already tells me not to trust the array approach at line 8:32. If the per-field read still fails, I skip the internals and clone the reference components (1:23, 1:26, 1:33, 1:44, 1:46 and the media components) into the 03 · Workspace page as an Assets section, then build instances from the clones; cloned components keep their image fill hashes, so the visuals match without reading properties. From the screenshot: Button is #1E32FA, radius ~26, white \"Get Started\" Semi Bold 15px, 358x52; Text Field has a bold 12px \"Phone Number\" label, white fill, 1px light border, radius 8, height 50, grey placeholder.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9717,"cache_read_input_tokens":32778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9717,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"359b0325-1852-491e-a496-b61dcab9b9f5"